  "body": "## Request\n\nRefresh the user documentation for the next release cut. Many features merged to `main` after `v0.27.0`, and the user guide does not describe all of them.\n\n## Work\n\n1. List the user-visible changes since `v0.27.0`: the `Changelog:` lines of the PRs merged after the tag (`git log --merges v0.27.0..main`, then each PR body), and the `feat` commits.\n2. For each user-visible change, find the page in `docs/user-guide/` that covers that area. Update the page, or add a short page when no page covers it. Describe behaviour only: what the user sees and does.\n3. Do not document internal changes (tests, refactors, process files, CI).\n4. Keep each page in its current style. Write new text in ASD-STE100.\n5. Docs only: no code, no snapshot PNGs, no `CHANGELOG.md` (the cut writes it).\n\nDone means: each user-visible change since `v0.27.0` has its description in `docs/user-guide/`, and the PR body lists the changes with the page that covers each.\n\nTiming: the maintainer prepares a release cut. Open the PR as soon as the pages are done, so it can merge before the cut starts.\n",
